  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is a constructor?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A constructor is a special method called when an object is created. It initializes the object's state and ensures valid initial values."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Constructors have the same name as the class and no return type. Can be parameterized or parameterless. Constructor chaining allows reusing initialization logic."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Constructor Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public class Person {\n    public string Name { get; set; }\n    public int Age { get; set; }\n    \n    // Default constructor\n    public Person() { }\n    \n    // Parameterized constructor\n    public Person(string name, int age) {\n        Name = name;\n        Age = age;\n    }\n}"
      }
    },
